<StaticPageLayout
  title="Corrections"
  eyebrow="ACCURACY"
  description="How LUDIVON handles factual errors, outdated guidance and reader-reported problems."
>
  <h2>Our commitment to accuracy</h2>

  <p>
    We aim to publish guidance that is accurate, useful and
    appropriately qualified. However, technical information
    can change, and mistakes can occur.
  </p>

  <p>
    When an article contains a material error or becomes outdated,
    we aim to review the issue and correct the information clearly.
  </p>

  <h2>What should be reported?</h2>

  <p>
    Readers can report issues such as:
  </p>

  <ul class="policy-list">
    <li>Incorrect technical claims or specifications.</li>
    <li>Instructions that no longer work or produce misleading results.</li>
    <li>Compatibility information that is incomplete or inaccurate.</li>
    <li>Performance claims that lack adequate supporting evidence.</li>
    <li>Broken sources or references.</li>
    <li>Material information that has become outdated.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information that helps us investigate</h2>

  <p>
    A useful correction report should include as much of the
    following as possible:
  </p>

  <ol class="policy-list">
    <li>The URL of the affected article.</li>
    <li>The heading, paragraph or instruction that needs review.</li>
    <li>A description of what appears to be wrong.</li>
    <li>The relevant device, Android version or game version, if applicable.</li>
    <li>Supporting documentation, screenshots or reliable sources, where available.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>How corrections are handled</h2>

  <p>
    Reported issues should be assessed against reliable evidence
    and the context of the original guidance.
  </p>

  <p>
    Substantive corrections should be reflected in the article.
    Where appropriate, the article's update date and correction
    explanation should also be revised.
  </p>

  <p>
    Minor typographical or formatting corrections may be made
    without a separate correction notice when they do not alter
    the meaning of the guidance.
  </p>

  <h2>Outdated information</h2>

  <p>
    Gaming and technology information can change following
    software updates, game patches, device releases and
    platform changes.
  </p>

  <p>
    When a change materially affects an article, the relevant
    information should be reviewed and updated. If the guidance
    can no longer be relied upon, it should be corrected,
    qualified or withdrawn from normal publication.
  </p>

  <h2>Report an issue</h2>

  <div class="prelaunch-note">
    <p>
      <strong>Pre-launch contact notice:</strong>
      LUDIVON's verified public contact channel has not yet
      been added. It will be published before public launch.
    </p>

    <p>
      Until that channel is available, this page describes
